=== 40bdd23edf
nup: boot update-only containers against a companion base NUP

An update-only container (standalone_update) is a patch, not a complete
game: booting its program without the base leads to code running against
missing content - black screen at 0 fps with unmapped reads long after a
successful ExeFS load (#333). The loader previously logged that it was
booting a standalone update and went ahead regardless.

When only an update package is present, look for a companion base .nup
in the same directory (exact title-ID match, then update & ~0x800 for
base/update ID pairs) and use it for the program identity, metadata and
base RomFS; the update still supplies the patched ExeFS and the RomFS
overlay already merges both trees. Legitimately complete standalone
containers keep booting as before. When no companion exists, keep the
attempt but log a warning explaining that a patch-only container needs
its base NUP instead of failing silently.

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine a9226c654316c9aaa548240f0f7725220e8b986d

