=== 9c2afa745e
settings: give Switch 2 titles their own CPU and graphics settings

Settings tuned for a Switch 2 title changed Switch 1 titles too. The saved
CPU and graphics settings (CPU, CPU unsafe, Renderer, Advanced, Hacks,
Extensions) now have two global profiles: Switch 1 in [Cpu]/[Renderer]
as before, Switch 2 in [Switch2Cpu]/[Switch2Renderer]. The settings hold
the active profile and the other one is kept aside; per-game values are
not part of a profile, so a game's own settings still apply on top of
its console's profile.

Qt (before the render target is made), eden-cli (before the command line
and the window) and System::Load switch to the Switch 2 profile for a
program whose main.npdm has the Switch 2 ACID layout, and back when the
game stops. Config IO and the dialog never swap: each profile is read and
written as its own, whichever is live, so the profile not in use can be
changed while a game runs. A configuration without the Switch 2 sections
starts the Switch 2 profile as a copy of the current settings.

The configuration dialog gets a Switch 2 Settings entry: CPU, Graphics,
Advanced and Extras tabs for the Switch 2 profile (the same tab classes,
built with a builder for that profile), and Switch 2 and Debug tabs for
settings only Switch 2 titles use, promoted from environment variables
that still win when set: GPU thread split (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT), forced swap
interval (EDEN_NX2_SWAP_INTERVAL), temporal upscale in place of DLSS
(EDEN_NX2_TEMPORAL_UPSCALE), idle core spin (EDEN_NX2_IDLE_SPIN_US),
mesh shaders (EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH) and a video memory limit
(EDEN_NX2_VRAM_LIMIT_MIB). A Switch 2 title's per-game properties show
the Switch 2 profile as its global values.

Frame generation's optical flow interpolation blended the current frame
with itself: after measuring the flow it copied the new frame over the
history too. Keep the last two frames in two slots, move the images out
of UNDEFINED before use, keep the motion vectors in the layout their
descriptors name, give the generated frame the barriers LSFG uses, and
use a descriptor set per slot and presentation frame instead of
rewriting one that earlier frames may still use.

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine 93a63c48d6a0414673f625789ba6d14ce3061318

=== d2f50d0c84
loader: don't layer the Edition add-on over a Switch 1 program's RomFS

NSMB Wonder's Switch 2 Edition add-on is the data of the game's Switch 2
program: its tables are Product.110.Nin_Ounce_NVN2 and about 8,400 of its
files replace the Switch 1 ones with Switch 2 builds. The Switch 1 program
(1.0.0 and 1.2.0) names its data with Nin_NX_NVN only and has no NVN2
code, so with the layer it read Switch 2 files it cannot parse and called
through a null object in its BYML reader. Without it, the Switch 1
program runs as before, told it runs on a Switch 2 and that it has the
add-on (which it only counts).

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine f6e4a3852fc82017545dd0905a497e35c55d3e3a

