=== e5e4a10937
loader: Switch 2 Edition support (off by default) and add-on content from NUPs

A Switch 2 Edition of a Switch 1 game asks nn::pl::IsRunningOnOunce whether
it runs on a Switch 2 before it uses its Switch 2 Edition content. In the
SDK that function is a stub returning false (mov w0, wzr; ret), which the
console answers with true. With "Run Switch 2 Editions of Switch 1 games"
on (Switch 2 Settings > Switch 2), the NSO loader patches the stub to
return true, marks a program whose main imports it as a Switch 2 Edition
and gives it the Switch 2 settings, unless they use another graphics API
than the window was made for.

NSMB Wonder only counts its add-ons (nn::aoc::CountAddOnContent) and
reads everything through its own RomFS, and its Edition add-on mirrors
that RomFS (with Nin_Ounce_NVN2 files), so a Switch 2 Edition's NUP add-on
packages are layered over the base and update RomFS.

NUP containers now also hand their add-on packages to the program:
aoc:u counts and lists them, and fsp-srv OpenDataStorageByDataId opens
their RomFS (built from the package's tree). CountAddOnContent logs the
count it reports.

Off by default: with the Edition content, Wonder 1.2.0 writes into a null
object in its BYML reader about 7 s after boot and jumps to address 0
(also with the 8 GB memory layout).

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine 78af52ece3e80d88349a93c86e222a8d1930cc41

