=== ba73c42283
nx2: run the guest counter at 31.25 MHz for Switch 2 titles

The Switch 2 counter runs at 31.25 MHz and its SDK converts ticks with
that constant: Mario Kart World's sdk builds 31,250,000 in
nn::os::GetSystemTickFrequency, TickManager::ConvertToTimeSpan and
TickManager::ConvertToTick (19.2 MHz appears nowhere). Eglantine counted
at the Switch 1 rate for every title, so every tick-based time in a
Switch 2 game was off by 1.63x: elapsed times read short, and a deadline
of one 60 Hz frame converted to ticks waited ~27 ms.

The wall clock now has a guest counter frequency, set at boot: 31.25 MHz
for Switch 2 programs, 19.2 MHz otherwise, EDEN_NX2_CNTFRQ=<Hz> to force
one. CNTPCT reads, CNTFRQ_EL0, svcGetSystemTick, thread tick counts and
the time services' tick conversions follow it.

Mario Kart World, title screen and attract demo, 180 s, same build:
frame times unchanged (17-19 ms once warm), process CPU time 848 s
instead of 930 s.

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine bc757f62d7db03674de9d790661c15e9279cbd81

