=== 9319953af4
[ci] gate pull requests on Linux and Windows

The repository had zero workflows and zero runs, so nothing checked that a change
still compiles. Meanwhile the compiler matrix is asymmetric: GCC and Clang are built
with `-Werror=all,extra,shadow,unused,conversion`, MSVC explicitly disables
warnings-as-errors. A Linux-green change can be Windows-broken, and a Windows-green
change can be Linux-red. Neither leg is redundant.

Six jobs: branch-name, lint (headers, spelling, whitespace, adapter cap, TEMP budget),
linux-gcc, linux-clang, windows-msvc, and an overlap report that comments which files a
PR shares with other open PRs. The compile legs use the dependency-light ci-core presets
so all three runners stay cheap; Qt and packaging parity run nightly.

required status checks are an owner action and deliberately not part of this change.

Assisted-by: Hermes Agent (deepseek-v4.1-flash) (drafted the change; human review required)

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine 91404dcda3b341093a3865e0ed5e39579c874469

