=== 77d06001be
Handle Pokopia shader address arithmetic and convergence escapes

The post-character-creation vertex shader uses LEA.HI with a nonzero
base, nested BREAK/move/BRA escapes, and full-mask WARPSYNC. Preserve
that arithmetic, retire the convergence token on the escape edge,
and emit an explicit subgroup execution barrier for Vulkan.

Restrict BREAK to the verified predicated move/escape sequence and
reject partial warp masks. OpenGL backends reject subgroup barriers
explicitly until equivalent support is implemented.

Validation: Eden2 build passed; focused arithmetic/control-flow/SPIR-V
and private captured-shader tests passed 163 assertions. Native shader
suite: 72 of 73 cases passed, 12027 of 12028 assertions. The existing
DNZ rejection test also fails on the previous commit's lowering code.
The Eglantine master rebase itself has not been built yet.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex (debugging, implementation and tests)

Ported-from: https://github.com/Djihads80/Eglantine 1d13ec49f8ddd77a0a143a04ed4267c148b4ca6e

=== 078dc10392
Support negated addends in native immediate IMAD

Pokopia's post-character-creation shader uses IMAD.IADD with a negated
register addend. Materialize its modular negation before lowering the
multiply-add so the shader is accepted with the intended arithmetic.

The focused integer multiplication regression passed 86 assertions.
The Eden2 executable rebuilt; the Eglantine rebase remains unbuilt.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex (diagnosis, implementation and regression test)

