=== a5695abac8
[hle] constexpr handler dispatch maps, introduce version gating (#4480)

This PR primarily focuses on upbringing constexpr maps for handlers.

Each time an HLE object of a service is construed, it registers it's own handlers, over and over.
Regardless of whetever it needs them at the moment or not.
Additionally we don't require to keep track of different function pointers amongst each object.
This can be done by overriding the given function instead, as opposed to having a separate
hash map for every given object.

In other words: Remove handlers (and handlers_tipc) map for every instance
then read from a static defined per-class.

- [x] Migrate all HLE functions to new `frozen::map` constexpr time finder
- [ ] Measure if this approach actually makes better codegen

Optional:
- [x] Properly gate all functions (that have versions commented next to them)
- [x] Maybe store `HandlerFnP<>` and `const char*` separately, version gating can go in a different map as well

Information such as name can be used on debug builds, but doesn't particularly help on release as one can consult an external reference (or have an annotated IPC map)

