=== 688c6fa7d8
vk_pipeline_cache: rebuild compute pipelines once a null pointer slot holds a buffer

Native compute programs take their storage buffer pointers from constant
buffer slots, and storage tracking only binds a slot that holds a mapped
address when the program is translated. A slot that is still null then
gets no binding, and the environment saved to the disk cache keeps that
answer, so every later session builds the program the same way.

In Ocarina of Time the foliage list compute was first built in a scene
where two of its list pointers were null. In Hyrule Castle Town those
lists exist, but the cached program never wrote them, the passes that
build the near bush and hedge leaves never ran, and the bushes stayed
bare brown twigs up close (green from afar, a different LOD). Turning the
disk shader cache off hid it.

Remember which pointer slots a compute pipeline left out because they
were null, check them when the program is dispatched again, and rebuild
it once one holds a mapped address. The rebuild keeps the slots the
previous build bound, so a slot that empties again doesn't start another
rebuild, and stops after four. The rebuilt record goes to the disk cache;
at load the record that binds more pointers wins, so the next session
starts with it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (debugging, implementation, drafting)
Signed-off-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>

