=== 18106bdf49
shader: split misaligned SSBO accesses, fix AMD depth sampling, CAS retries and shuffles

Ports the shader parts of zortos293/Lichii#295 and #273.

- 64 and 128-bit storage buffer accesses are split into 32-bit words when
  min_ssbo_alignment is smaller than the access, instead of using a u32x2/u32x4
  view that can start before the access. Covers direct offsets and the global
  memory functions.
- Depth-compare images stay float even when the descriptor reports an integer
  format.
- Failed compare-exchange results feed the next retry (storage, shared and
  narrow writes) instead of reloading a possibly stale word.
- Fragment-stage shuffles use the broadcast/select fallback on AMD's
  proprietary driver.

Launch gates, on by default and off with =0: EGLANTINE_SSBO_ALIGN_FIX,
EGLANTINE_DEPTH_FLOAT_FIX, EGLANTINE_CAS_RETRY_FIX. The first and last change
the emitted SPIR-V, so clear the shader cache when switching.

