=== a8edfd1bec
dynarmic: x64: fix VectorCountLeadingZeros16 on AVX-512

The AVX512CD path narrowed the eight 32-bit lzcnt results with a 128-bit
vpackusdw, which only reads four of them, so the upper four lanes of CLZ Vd.8H
came back as 0xfff0 on every CPU with AVX-512. libjpeg's NEON Huffman encoder
uses that instruction for coefficient bit lengths, which corrupted the
JPEG thumbnail the game writes with a save (valid file, noise below the first
rows). Narrow with vpmovdw instead. The existing "A64: CLZ" dynarmic test
fails on AVX-512 hosts without this and passes with it.

Ported from zortos293/Lichii#8.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5

=== 3f7bcc5b8d
Merge pull request #715 from Djihads80/fix/oot-near-leaves

shader: bind loaded pointers that compete with a paired cbuf pointer
=== a51a69fbfb
shader: bind loaded pointers that compete with a paired cbuf pointer

A native global access whose address is a select or phi of a constant
buffer pointer and a pointer loaded from that buffer was paired with the
constant buffer pointer alone, so the native candidate search never ran.
Accesses through the loaded pointer were then rebased on the constant
buffer's binding and read out of bounds as zeros.

Ocarina of Time reads its foliage unit placement records from c0[12] or
from *c0[12]. The near-leaf pass (539ffb3f650a34ac) read every record as
zero, normalised a zero vector and wrote NaN positions, so the near
ShootLeaf meshes (BancLeafMesh, FoliageLeafNear) were never built and
trees lost their leaves inside about 20 m.

Run the candidate search for paired accesses too. If a loaded pointer
competes with the pair, bind every candidate plus the paired pointer and
let the backend pick the buffer at run time; otherwise keep the pair.

Signed-off-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>

