=== 7b1aeff913
nvdrv: count command list entries copied after a queued GPU map

Logs the first eight entries that are behind a queued map, then every thousandth, with the number of entries seen, so a log shows whether a title ever submits a list over a pending map.

(cherry picked from commit eeb09ff35206d9f052176352698e7db317030be4)

=== 2c9263140d
dma_pusher: count entries parsed from memory that differ from their submit-time copy

An entry read from memory instead of its submit snapshot is how a command ring the game already refilled gets read as this frame's commands. Log, by the reason the snapshot was skipped (resumed entry, copied during a suspension, suspension count changed, GPU-written page, safe read of dirty memory), how often the words differ. Bounded to the first 50000 such entries, four warnings per reason, a summary every 10000.

(cherry picked from commit e17076e388b42506a7f006ebc7af02bcff07f0d9)

=== 49d1e8cb74
nvdrv: keep submit-time copies of entries no pending map covers

The previous commit skipped the submit-time copy of every entry while any
GPU map was queued. A list in a command ring that was mapped long before
then ran from memory again, which a game may already be refilling for a
later frame: the case the copies are there for.

MapInOrder now takes the GPU address range a map changes, and the GPU
keeps the ranges queued and not done yet. Only an entry overlapping one
is left out (CommandList::deferred_entries) and read from memory until
DmaPusher::Push copies it after the maps; the others are copied at
submit as before. A full refresh (a resume from a suspension) copies the
deferred entries too.

Pokopia defers 7 entries in a minute, its first lists after mapping
their memory, and runs on JIT at High and Low; a check comparing each
parsed copy with memory found no difference.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (review follow-up, implementation and testing)
(cherry picked from commit e731d0201039b49a718f05675ce60c074a72babb)

=== 74cd3b432e
nvdrv: copy command lists submitted behind a queued GPU map later

Pokopia stopped at its first frame since 9fea7d8379. GMMU maps run in
order on the GPU thread (GPU::MapInOrder), but the copy of a command
list taken at submit reads through the GPU addresses at once, on the
service thread. Pokopia submits its first lists on a channel right after
mapping their memory: they were copied before the map ran, as zeros,
and the channel ran nothing.

Before 9fea7d8379 the suspension count changed at nearly every entry,
so these copies were mostly ignored and the lists were read from memory.
Now that the count is right, every list runs from its copy.

The GPU now counts the maps queued and not done yet. With one pending,
the submit leaves the copy out and marks it out of date; DmaPusher::Push
takes it on the GPU thread, after the maps.

Pokopia now runs on JIT at High and Low, where it stopped at frame 1. A
check comparing each list's copy with memory as it is parsed found no
difference, where it found Pokopia's first lists all zeros before.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (bisect, diagnosis, fix and testing)
(cherry picked from commit 11bc11d685422732a2f10f0a8988628e35f1071d)

=== bc121caf3e
vulkan: keep task and mesh pipelines in their own disk cache file

Task and mesh programs are translated with the mesh registers and the
pass-through header, which vulkan.bin records don't carry, so pipelines
with them (Ocarina's terrain and foliage) were built again in every session.
They now go to vulkan_mesh.bin with that state and boot loads them from
there; task/mesh records in vulkan.bin are skipped. Builds without this
change never open the new file, so the cache version stays the same.

Based on Frizti/Lichii 3a2c8980ad.

