=== d713f4462a
video_core: reuse the last memory layout interval during draw setup

GetMemoryLayoutSize repeats a std::map search for index sizing and storage-buffer descriptors even when addresses stay inside the same layout interval. Retain that interval by value and return its end minus the queried address on a hit. Every Map/Unmap invalidates it, including updates that split, merge or extend adjacent intervals.

The lookup is explicitly non-const because it updates the cache. MemoryManager keeps the same guard around both queries and mapping changes; no locks or GPU synchronization are skipped. This is the only production RangeMap consumer. A page-independent array oracle checks sizes across 20,000 randomized remaps, holes, boundary queries and repeated lookups.

Cherry-picked from zortos293/Lichii 6242f664dafc219429cb4753f5db6675858e70c7.

