=== 5512454976
kepler_compute: stand in for Mario Kart World's docked photo mode upscale

Docked, the photo mode renders at 2560x1440 and upscales to 3840x2160 with a
network of tensor-core passes. Those passes are rejected (native matrix
multiply), so the 4K image stayed empty and only the UI drawn over it showed.

The existing fallback only looks at a few fixed constant buffer slots of the
rejected pass. For this game it found no pair there and fell through to its
generic scan, which blitted unrelated small textures. When it does not handle
a rejected pass, the next 64 dispatches are now searched, in every constant
buffer, for a block-linear colour image and one 1.5 times its size; the pass
that has both has its result replaced by a bilinear blit of the first to the
second. The pass and the offsets are remembered, so later frames read only
those two handles, and the search stops after a few evaluations without a
match. The generic scan also ignores outputs under 1024 texels wide, which
are look-up tables and not upscale targets.

EDEN_NX2_PHOTO_UPSCALE=0 in nx2_switches.txt turns the stand-in off.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (root-cause analysis from logs, implementation)

=== 7f6f1d1289
externals: FFmpeg with AV1 on MinGW Windows

The MinGW builds (windows-x86_64-pgo) still used crueter-ci's FFmpeg,
which has no AV1 decoder, so Switch 2 movies in AV1 (Fire Emblem:
Fortune's Weave, the Ocarina of Time title screen) played black there
while the MSVC and Linux builds play them since 959973a76a. The log
showed nx2 video: FFmpeg has no decoder for "video/av1".

MinGW amd64 now uses the same FFmpeg as Takoroka/ffmpeg-av1 9.0.2-av1-1:
FFmpeg 946fcce07b with crueter-ci's patch and configure flags, plus
libdav1d 1.5.4 (MSYS2's static build) merged into libavcodec. The
package is a release of this repository (9.0.2-av1-mingw-1); its README
lists the sources and flags and it includes the build script. MSYS2's
dav1d is built with -fstack-protector-strong and _FORTIFY_SOURCE, so the
package also links mingw-w64's static libssp. ARM64 MinGW keeps
crueter-ci's package.

Tested on a local MinGW clang PGO build (RTX 5080), Ocarina of Time,
30 s from boot with no input: "Using decoder libdav1d" and the title
screen's AV1 movie plays; before, the decoder failed to open and the
frames stayed black. The binary links without new DLLs.

