=== 226f92afdb
vk_scheduler: pause, don't reset, the occlusion counter at each submission (Ocarina white flashes) (#121)

* vk_scheduler: pause, don't reset, the occlusion counter at each submission

EndPendingOperations runs before every Vulkan submission and reset the
ZPassPixelCount64 counter there (since Eden b1f3b568fb). A guest that resets
the counter, draws, and reports expects the report to cover every draw since
its own reset. When a submission lands between those draws and the report,
the reset drops the samples counted so far and the report reads too low.

The split GPU thread batches fence and command-list submissions on the back
thread (EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US), and other threads can force a pending flush
at any ring entry, so submissions now land mid-sequence often. In Ocarina of
Time (0400486024DEC000) this shows as one-frame white flashes on Link.

Pause the counter instead, as yuzu did, and keep the query running across
the submission. EndRenderPass already pauses it at render pass end, the next
draw resumes it, and the guest's own reset still clears it.

Tested in Kokiri Forest (RTX 4090, Low GPU accuracy, split=2), 36 s of
consecutive frames with Link on screen, same binary with a temporary switch:
old reset 15 and 9 flashes, this change 0 and 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* vk_query_cache: bound the running occlusion query across submissions

Since the counter is paused instead of reset at each submission, the host
query runs until the guest resets or reports the counter. Ocarina of
Time's title screen and file select keep ZPass counting on and do
neither, so the query grew by a slot at every submission and render
pass. By the time gameplay started it held 16,384 slots over all 64
sample banks, and a running query keeps every bank it touches alive. On
AMD with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2 the game then hung right after picking the
save, with WaitSubmitted waiting on a tick the GPU thread never
submitted (reported on zortos293/Lichii#121).

Once the running query passes one bank (256 slots), drop the count as a
reset would. In gameplay the longest reset-to-report window measured was
36 slots over 4 submissions (1.36M reports), so real windows keep the
carried count.

Tested on RTX 4090, Low accuracy, EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2,
EDEN_NX2_FENCE_BATCH=1. With logging on, the query stayed within two
banks through the title screen and file select, and gameplay windows
were unchanged. Outside Link's house, 36 s of consecutive frames with
Link on screen: 0 flashes in 576 frames, 60.5 fps.
tests.exe: 651 of 654 pass, the same 3 known failures as before. The
hang itself doesn't reproduce on NVIDIA, so the AMD retest is pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

