=== 954985d351
shader: fold multiplies by 0 and 1 again so Ocarina's sky ambient binds its buffer

Re-applies b1a0e3fbf8, which 270732f525 reverted.

Ocarina of Time's sky ambient compute (b76d7b3e9e93093d, one 32x32 group per
frame) samples the sky texture and atomically adds 12 floats (sky spherical
harmonics, RGB x L0+L1) into a small frame buffer that the scene materials and
the fog read. The guest builds the address as IMAD.WIDE pointer * 1 + offset,
with the pointer at c0+0x20 and the offset (0x30) in c1[0].

The XMAD lowering of "* 1" leaves lo16*1 + ((hi16*1 + lo16*0) << 16), and
constant propagation only folds IMul32 when both operands are immediates. The
pointer stays hidden behind the unfolded halves, so storage buffer tracking
sees c1[0] as the only addend, keeps it as the atomic's pointer, and the
binding reads 0x30 as an address: a null buffer, every add dropped, the sky
ambient zero.

IMul32 by 0 or 1 now folds, and (bfe(a,16,16) << 16) + bfe(a,0,16) folds back
to a, so the tracker finds c0+0x20. In a frame dump the dispatch has its
256-byte storage binding again and readers get (6.5, 8.4, 12.9) for the L0
term instead of zeros. Pipeline cache versions bumped (Vulkan 26, OpenGL 23).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (debugging, implementation)

