=== fe2cd8be2b
buffer_cache: don't download GPU data over newer CPU writes

With asynchronous GPU emulation, Ocarina of Time's Z-target reticle jumped
back and forth: on about half of the frames (56-67 % with a dynamic-fps mod,
25-28 % stock) it was drawn at the angle of two frames before while the rest
of the frame was current. Turning asynchronous GPU emulation off fixed it.

The reticle is a particle effect whose per-frame emitter constants the game
writes into double-buffered slots of a buffer the GPU also writes. CPU writes
into GPU-written memory are only collected when they happen; the GPU thread
applies them later (InvalidateGPUCache). Until then they are guest memory the
buffer cache doesn't know about, and two download paths wrote the GPU's older
copy over them:

- The fencing thread writes finished async downloads back while the CPU keeps
  running. A write collected after the download was taken isn't removed from
  it until the GPU thread applies it, so the download landed on top.
- Applying the collected writes one by one: WriteMemory downloads the
  GPU-written bytes elsewhere on the pages it touches, which included the
  next collected write on the same page.

OoT presents a frame ahead (its GPU waits on semaphores the CPU releases
later), so the CPU writes the next frame's slots while the GPU thread still
works on this one, and the slot it had just written reverted to the value
from two frames before.

Now:
- Every guest-memory write of downloaded data skips the CPU writes collected
  and not yet applied (GPUDirtyMemoryManager::ForEachPending reads them
  without consuming them).
- InvalidateGPUCache hands the collected writes to the rasterizer as one
  batch; the Vulkan rasterizer takes all of them out of the GPU-written
  ranges before applying any.

Synchronous GPU emulation and the frames-ahead present wait are unchanged.

OoT (v131072, docked, CLI harness, ZL held at the training scarecrow, Dynamic
FPS mod): reticle flips back in 0 % of frames (before: 56-67 %), frame time
37.7 ms (before: 35-40 ms).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (debugging, implementation)
Signed-off-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit e27fbc6b037915af845f0566a2d6c56126a6479f)

