=== 9a69d8eaf0
shader: lower Ocarina's byte uniform loads, ULEA carries, F2IP pairs and I2F.U8 of a UR byte

Distant (LOD) vegetation in Ocarina of Time flashed white for a frame
now and then. Five of its compute programs were rejected and skipped on
every dispatch (60 failed dispatches a second):

- ULDC.U8/U16 (c[0x4][UR6+0x82]): ULDC took only 32/64-bit loads.
  LDC has the byte and halfword sizes; a direct offset is aligned to
  the size, an indexed one only as a sum (ULDC UR7, c[0x4][UR15+0x29]).
- ULEA UR10, UP3, ...: the carry is computed in P(6-n) and merged into
  R239 like UISETP, so any UPn works, not only UP0/UP1.
- F2IP.U8.F32 Rd, Ra, Rb, RZ: two bytes packed, Rb low (Duck912's
