=== df92fc6c95
nx2: keep other threads out of the Vulkan scheduler while the split's back submits

Two paths from #494 let a second thread use the scheduler at the same time as
the GPU back thread, which crashed in Scheduler::SubmitExecution (SIGSEGV,
SEGV_MAPERR, from GpuSplit::BackLoop -> Scheduler::FlushDeferred) in Mario
Kart World and other games.

- The back runs its idle hook (the deferred fence / list-copy flush) after it
  has published everything as consumed, so GpuSplit::Drain() could return and
  the front run work of its own (MapInOrder) while that submit was going on.
  The back now clears back_quiet before it executes entries and sets it after
  the idle hook; Drain() waits for it as well and asks the back to run the
  hook at once when it is still spinning.
- BufferCache::WriteMemory downloads the GPU-written bytes on written pages
  (b13c4c1c0c), which records and submits work. Device memory unmaps and
  writes, ThreadManager::InvalidateRegion and FlushAndInvalidateRegion reach it
  on CPU and service threads. It now downloads only on the thread that owns
  the scheduler (GpuSplit::OwnsScheduler: the back while it runs, else the GPU
  thread). Guest CPU writes still go through TryCacheInvalidation, which sends
  such pages to the GPU thread.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (diagnosis from tester stack traces, fix)

=== 90ff431884
puller: release fences again while an acquire waits with delayed fence operations

With Balanced GPU fences Ocarina of Time froze after a while: channel 2
waited on a semaphore 0x13 releases behind ("waits on semaphore ...
(0xdc19, now 0xdc06)") and no channel moved again.

A semaphore release is a payload query, which delayed fence operations
(Balanced or Accurate fences, accurate GPU) keep in the query cache until
the next fence. An acquire releases the fences once and then suspends the
channel, and the recheck only read the semaphore: a release queued after
that waited for a fence nobody made, with every channel suspended. The
recheck now releases the fences again, at most once a millisecond, while
operations are delayed. Default fences are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude

=== 1b594aa6b6
fence_manager: submit deferred work before waiting on our own fence

With Balanced GPU fences Ocarina of Time froze loading a save (0 fps):
the fencing thread waited forever for a tick ("Waited N s for the GPU
thread to submit tick ...").

The puller's fence acquire and syncpoint waits run ReleaseFences on the
GPU split's back: WaitPendingFences(true) signals a fence and blocks until
the fencing thread has run its callback. With delayed fence operations
(Balanced, Accurate, or accurate GPU) the callback waits for the fence's
tick, but the back deferred that tick's submission (DeferFlush) to its
idle hook, which it never reached while blocked. With Default fences the
callback ran inside SignalFence, so the wait never blocked.

The waiter now submits deferred work before it blocks. Balanced fences
load the save and run; fence behaviour Default is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude

