skills: switch GPU accuracy from the lab; split restart verification

=== 2cb4cc8bbb
video_core: release fences that carry downloads after the downloads land (#72)

Without fence delays (GPU accuracy Low, the default fence behaviour), a
fence's guest-visible operation (semaphore or query release, syncpoint)
ran when the fence was signalled, while the buffer and texture downloads
committed with it reached guest memory only when the fence popped. A guest
that saw the fence could read the bytes the downloads were about to
replace.

On nx2 the buffer cache downloads at fences only ranges the guest CPU has
read before, so this affects GPU readbacks. Yoshi and the Mysterious Book
panics in Unreal's distance field streaming, which reads its streaming
requests from a GPU readback ring; stale requests there are the suspected
cause.

A fence that commits downloads now queues its operation behind them, as
fences already do with delays on. Fences with nothing to download are
released at once as before. EDEN_NX2_DOWNLOAD_FENCE=0 restores the old
order for comparisons.

