=== 66b9ff826f
engines: hand the macros back to the engines when the GPU split stops

Switching the GPU accuracy fast -> accurate -> fast mid-game stopped and
restarted the split, and Ocarina of Time then hung on the next rupee
pickup: a fence waited forever for the GPU thread ("Waited N s for the GPU
thread to submit tick ...").

The first front macro call copies an engine's registers, shadow RAM and
macro state to the split's front (Front) and sets front_macros, which
makes the engine skip macro uploads and binds. Stopping the split never
undid that: while stopped the engine dropped the game's macro uploads and
binds, and the restarted front kept its copy from before the stop. With
EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY=1 the front's 3D registers differed from the
engine's in 7 places right after the restart (0 before the switch).

The first engine method run off the split's back (the split has stopped)
now moves the macro state back to the engine and drops the front's copy;
a restart copies afresh. After the same switch: 0 differences in 23,809
checks.

Assisted-by: Claude

=== 65e5b1011d
skills: OoT white wash comes from culled vegetation; split check on Linux

=== 4ac9e703fe
shader, video_core: bind storage buffers behind loaded pointers for OoT's vegetation

Ocarina of Time culls its vegetation on the GPU: compute programs read
instance transforms through a pointer loaded from memory a constant buffer
points to, and write per-type task counts that the task and mesh draws
read; the vegetation shaders read instance and material data through
pointer tables. The storage buffer pass could not follow those pointers,
so the loads read 0: every instance was culled, grass and broad-leaf
plants never drew, and bushes, vines and the door drew black. With the dark
canopy missing and the plants unlit the exposure ran away, and bloom and
haze washed out the scene.

Takes the storage buffer pass from Duck912's oot-build16 (1038827cf5),
which carries the Lichii pass generation and three changes on top:
- a compute program can load its buffer pointer from memory a constant
  buffer pointer points to (indirect_offset); the buffer cache reads the
  holder at bind time and the SPIR-V backend picks the closest base through
  the holder's binding (Lichii 88b158a80d),
- the candidate walk follows ShuffleIndex (R2UR); table pointers packed
  whole, phis or selects of them, and constant buffer arrays indexed at
  run time are candidates in compute, within the bindings left free; and
  graphics stages bind a pointer read from a table at a fixed offset,
- read-only table pointers bind to the end of their mapping, up to 64 MiB:
  the grass records lie 11.7 to 17.7 MiB past the pool's base.

Our pass held nothing the taken one lacks: its memory-load stop
(461015ea5f) is upstream's and still passes its test. Not taken: the
coherent global memory flag the pass merged (no such feature here), and
Duck's sub-mapping walk; table pointers use MaxContinuousRange like native
ones. Pipeline cache versions bumped (Vulkan 24, OpenGL 21).

Kokiri Forest from the same save: the white wash and the black plant
silhouettes are gone, grass and broad-leaf plants draw on the verges and
ledges, and luma holds at 0.55-0.65 while walking instead of swinging from
0.84 to 0.43. A five-minute walk ran without faults at the same frame time.

Ported from Duck912 56e599c57d, 50578e4c3c and 1038827cf5; jojo-chaechae's
oot-jojo takes the same route (88b158a80d, 220a985a7c).

Co-authored-by: Jonas <baguettegamerofficial2020@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude (port)

