=== 3087c1cf07
video_core: run the front's fence work, macro DMA flushes and maps on the split's back

Ocarina of Time crashed a few seconds into walking around, on the GPU
thread's front: a GP entry with its sync bit drained the back and then
called SignalFence there. Its InvalidateGPUCache uploaded the CPU's writes
over GPU-written pages (WriteMemory, InlineMemoryImplementation,
CopyBuffer) into the scheduler while the drained back's idle hook
(Scheduler::FlushDeferred) swapped the command chunk: a read at null+0x10
in BufferCacheRuntime::CopyBuffer. The previous change moved the front's
other flushes to the back and missed these.

The same now goes through GpuSplit::Run in each place the front used
back-owned state after a drain: a GP entry's sync fence (SignalFence), the
puller's acquire and release paths (ReleaseFences), the macro DMA read
flush (FrontDmaRead) and GPU memory maps (UnmapMemory downloads).

Ported from the fence part of Duck912 e3d8e9c605 (#70); its command page
drain changes and per-site wait profiling are not included.

