=== 34f24ae551
Revert "buffer_cache: bind native read-only storage buffers to the end of their mapping"

This reverts commit 1992f6ef990162a1cb26d999a952b76da4611625.

=== 1992f6ef99
buffer_cache: bind native read-only storage buffers to the end of their mapping

Ocarina of Time's grass reads per-blade instance records from a pool read
11.7 to 17.7 MiB past the binding's base (frame dump: 289 task groups of up
to 256 instances). A native pointer was bound with at most 8 MiB, robust
buffer access returned 0 for every record, the task shader culled every
blade and no grass drew, in the depth prepass and the colour pass alike.

Read-only native bindings now extend to the end of their mapping, up to
64 MiB; MaxContinuousRange stops them where the mapping does. Written
bindings keep the 8 MiB cap (a write marks the whole binding GPU-modified),
and so does every non-native pointer: raising the cap for all of them grew
hundreds of bindings into an 80 MiB region and slowed the game down.

Ported from Duck912 1038827cf5, which flags the pointers read from a table
explicitly; this tree cannot tell those apart until storage buffers behind
loaded pointers are tracked, so the cap follows the read-only flag.

Co-authored-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude (port)

=== b1a0e3fbf8
shader: fold multiplies by 0 and 1 so Ocarina's sky ambient binds its buffer

Ocarina of Time's sky ambient compute (b76d7b3e9e93093d, one 32x32 group per
frame) samples the sky texture and atomically adds 12 floats (sky spherical
harmonics, RGB x L0+L1) into a small frame buffer that the scene materials and
the fog read. The guest builds the address as IMAD.WIDE pointer * 1 + offset,
with the pointer at c0+0x20 and the offset (0x30) in c1[0].

The XMAD lowering of "* 1" leaves lo16*1 + ((hi16*1 + lo16*0) << 16), and
constant propagation only folded IMul32 when both operands were immediates. The
pointer stayed hidden behind the unfolded halves, so storage buffer tracking saw
c1[0] as the only addend, kept it as the atomic's pointer, and the binding read
0x30 as an address: a null buffer, every add dropped, the sky ambient zero.

IMul32 by 0 or 1 now folds, and (bfe(a,16,16) << 16) + bfe(a,0,16) folds back to
a. The tracker then finds c0+0x20. In a frame dump the dispatch now has its
256-byte storage binding and readers get (6.5, 8.4, 12.9) for the L0 term
instead of zeros; rock and shadow colours in Kokiri Forest turn less yellow. The
outdoor haze is unchanged. Pipeline cache versions bumped (Vulkan 51,
OpenGL 47) because translation output changes for any program with such
multiplies.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (debugging, implementation)
(cherry picked from commit 05435ee185268e4cb972eb3de00a611bed08c6f4)

=== 582ecc4568
shader: shadow ISBEWR data registers (Ocarina door NaN) (#100)

The register shadowing check reads bits 32-39 only for register-form
opcodes and a short list of exceptions, so ISBEWR's data register was
never considered. When a mesh program stores an attribute from a register
at or above the uniform bank (Ocarina's mesh 8159e91e0097876a stores
R238 and R240), the store read Lichii's own UR mirror instead of the
native value. RegisterPressure already lists 0x927 with operands 24 and 32;
it was just never asked.

In Ocarina, Link's house door got attribute 6 = (0, UR22's mirror), a bit
mask that reads as NaN; bloom turned the door into a white glow. With the
data register shadowed, the doorway has no NaN pixels and the gate renders.

Assisted by: Claude Code/Opus 5.5

(cherry picked from commit b328477840f24da9238b8ea3c17747e01b9b2a73)

