=== dbf3417099
video_core: upscale stand-in takes its images from the native program

When a tensor network is rejected, the stand-in blits its input to its
output. Outside the known slots it took the first same-format pair in
cbuf0+0x80..0x11c, which in Ocarina of Time's gameplay was a 4x4 image
onto a 1920x1080 target and a 120x67 one over the 2560x1440 frame: the
3D scene went black.

The handles the program itself reads (TEX/TLD/TLD4) and stores to
(SUST.P) through cbuf0 are tried first, and every pair must keep the
aspect ratio and scale by at most 4. Input and output may differ in
format, and an E5B9G9R9 input (no 2D surface format) is blitted
through a source format override in the texture cache, which on
Vulkan samples the source through a plain view.

Checked in game (hidden eden-cli, Kokiri Forest save): the scene draws
again without EDEN_NX2_TENSOR, as bright as the network's own output.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (found the wrong pairs, wrote the fix, ran the checks)

