=== 6b934346d7
shader: route untracked 32-bit global atomics to their storage buffer

Every SPIR-V global atomic threw "SPIR-V Instruction is not
implemented", so a compute program whose atomic address the storage
buffer pass could not track failed to build and its dispatches were
dropped (four Ocarina compute pipelines; the dumps show U32 ADD/MAX,
S32 MIN and F32 ADD reductions).

Each 32-bit global atomic the program uses now gets a function on the
routing global loads and stores already use: the address picks the
candidate storage buffer, and the operation runs on its word. INC, DEC
and F32 add go through the storage buffer CAS loops. 64-bit and packed
forms still throw.

The test emits each of the 12 operations untracked; the modules pass
spirv-val (Vulkan 1.1, standard uniform buffer layout).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (traced the pipeline failures, wrote the routing and test)

=== 19e25d0cfb
shader: lower the rest of Ocarina's dumped native programs

All 833 programs from an Ocarina shader dump now lower; the 800 that
already did lower to identical code.

- SGXT takes its signed form (bit 73) as BFE.S32.
- USHF.L.U32.HI with an immediate (0x499) lowers like SHF 0x419, with a
  UPn guard; Ocarina's mesh programs use it.
- UIADD3 carries go to and come from any UPn, through P(6-n) and R239 as
  UISETP does, not only UP0 and UP1.
- LEA.HI takes a negated Rb (bit 63) when it is not .X.
- SURED takes every op (bits 87-89), which Maxwell SURED reads in the
  same order at bits 24-26.
- Shadow operands for LDG, IADD3, FFMA, FMUL, FADD, FSEL, IMNMX, SGXT,
  S2R, ISETP and I2F forms the dump uses. An operand may no longer
  straddle the reserved boundary or span two borrowed quartets; either
  would be renamed to registers that are not adjacent.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (lowered the dump offline, decoded the rejections, wrote the fixes and tests)

=== f1a5c6e04f
shader: lower Ocarina 2D array, per-pixel offset and depth gathers

TLD4 accepted only plain 2D gathers with an optional AOFFI. Ocarina also
gathers from 2D arrays, with per-pixel offsets (bits 76-77 = 2) and with
a depth reference (bit 78). The source lists follow Mesa NAK: Ra holds
the coordinates with the array index first, Rb the offsets and then the
reference, and with nothing for Rb the coordinates split evenly across
both. Maxwell TLD4 reads the same lists, so the lowering copies them into
its coordinate and meta registers and sets the type, PTP and DC fields.

FMUL and FADD in register form get shadow operands for high registers.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (decoded the rejections from the log, wrote the lowering and tests)

