=== 4093f1529e
A game: boot and rendering fixes (#7)

* Fix a game startup crash and rejected I2F shaders

CircularBufferSinkInfo::CleanUp read its state as a DeviceState and freed
current_pos as an upsampler pointer when the game changed a sink's type.
Circular buffer sinks have no upsampler, so just clear the state.

Lower I2F.F32.S16 (bit 74 = signed source) and I2F.F32.U8 with a byte
selector instead of rejecting the shader.

* docs: A game bring-up notes on Linux

* ampere: lower ISETP.EX, REDUX.MIN and SHF with a constant source

A game (04007EF01F8AE000) dispatches all three on its first
frame; each was rejected as an unsupported mode, so the shaders were dropped and the
screen stayed black. The ISETP.EX and REDUX.MIN lowerings follow the same semantics
nxnative's translator implemented for the same title.

* ampere: lower the modes a game's first frames dispatch

IADD3.X with a constant source, LEA.HI.X, IMAD.HI with a constant multiplier and its .S32
sign, IMNMX with a 32-bit immediate, ATOMS.MIN/MAX, BAR.SYNC.DEFER_BLOCKING, BPT.TRAP as a
no-op, and LDG through desc[URn], which is a descriptor and not an address base.

* docs: FE bring-up state after the second lowering pass

* ampere: LEA.HI/HI.X with a register high word, stores through desc[URn]; docs

* video_core: separate surface and texture descriptor buffers; ampere: partial SUST.P masks, TXQ.B and the predicated NOINC call

* ampere: LEA with a carry predicate, F2I.U64, IMAD.X with a carry value, and the modifiers the first compute passes use

* docs: FE compute rejects after the second lowering pass

* ampere: IMAD.WIDE from partial products and a 64-bit constant addend

* docs: FE compute state after IMAD.WIDE

* ampere: IADD3 with one or two carry predicates and with a third-source carry-in

* ampere: LEA.HI.X with a constant base, HFMA2.RELU predicate output dropped, USHF over UR0-UR21, reserved-register destinations

* docs: the ten compute instructions a game still needs

* ampere: IDP.4A.S8.S8, LEA.HI with a uniform base, looser CALL linkage

* ampere: lower calls that sit in the captured library region

* docs: how to read an encoding out of turingas, and what MUFU operation 9 is

* ampere: I2F from a 64-bit unsigned pair, the second dot product form, IMAD modifiers, IADD3 bit 63

* kernel: let a same-core thread started before an IPC call run its entry code

A game starts one worker per core, passing each a pointer to an
argument block on the starting thread's stack. The core 0 worker has a lower
priority than the main thread and only runs once main blocks in IPC. On
hardware the IPC round trip leaves it enough time to read its arguments; HLE
services answer before it executed anything, main preempts it and reuses the
stack, and the worker later waits on a null barrier (address 0xc) forever,
hanging the boot at "Launching" in roughly half of all starts.

Keep the caller of SendSyncRequest blocked (a longer IPC latency is legal)
until such threads block on something other than a mutex or exit, bounded by
20 ms of host time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ampere: geometry exit analysis for F2I, LEA, LDC, LOP3, AST and exit handlers

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* texture_cache: split layered cross-format copies into per-layer copies

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* video_core: flush pending query reports before a native MME DMA read

The NX2 driver implements conditional rendering of a game's
characters (and the arena floor) in a macro that DMA-reads a ZPassPixelCount64
report. Only the buffer cache was flushed before the read, and the Vulkan
rasterizer never reported query cache regions as needing a flush, so the macro
saw 0 samples and disabled rendering for those draws.

Report query cache regions in MustFlushRegion and include the query cache in
the flush before the DMA read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ampere: uniform bindless TEX with LOD/bias and any mask; X8Z24 UNORM/UINT/UNORM/UNORM

A game's lighting compute shader samples with an explicit LOD
and an alpha-only mask through a uniform handle and has a WARPSYNC after
the sample; all three were rejected, so the dispatch was skipped and the
commentator window and character select stayed unlit. The X8Z24 depth view
with mixed components fell back to RGBA8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* maxwell_3d: flush query reports before a split-front MME DMA read

Same fix as the back path (7d19643e4): the front only flushed the buffer
cache, so occlusion-query-based conditional rendering read stale counts
with the GPU thread split and a game's characters vanished.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* dma_pusher: check GPU-written pages before draining the split back

The written-page bits never clear, so the check needs no drain; draining
first for every command list kept the split front waiting ~40% of the time
in a game (6M waits a minute). Only lists on written pages
drain and flush now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* game_settings: A game defaults to low GPU accuracy with balanced fences

Low accuracy enables the GPU thread split (about 30 to 60 fps in a match);
balanced fences keep occlusion reports in the query cache so the
conditional rendering behind the characters still sees them. Applied only
where the per-game setting is global, as the per-game value, so the user's
own choice wins and nothing is saved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ampere: fix the IMAD.WIDE lowering

- the high-word sum had no destination or predicate and OR-ed two source
  fields (wrote R0, read R254); it now goes to R249
- the high word was written to Rd, over the low word, instead of Rd+1
- the high word is computed before Rd is written, so Ra/Rb may alias Rd
- LDC read the addend at c[bank][R0 + offset]; the address register is RZ

Checked against a*b+c on an interpreter of the emitted Maxwell sequence
(aliasing and carry cases).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* texture_pass: storage images use the surface descriptor buffer

MakeInst runs before the opcode is indexed, so the ImageWrite check never
matched and surfaces always used the texture buffer. Classify with
IsStorageImageOpcode(IndexedInstruction(...)) (reads, writes, atomics).
Environments default surface_bound to ~0U (unset, falls back to the
texture buffer) instead of 0; the Vulkan (20) and OpenGL (16) cache
versions are bumped so caches that stored the 0 are dropped (OpenGL's was
never bumped when the field was added).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* kernel: read started threads under the scheduler lock, release them on finalize

The IPC wait read another core's thread state and waiting-lock info without
the scheduler lock, and a starter that exited without a later IPC call kept
its references to the started threads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* Fix native arithmetic, command synchronization and depth aliases

Co-authored-by: capy-ai[bot] <230910855+capy-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

* Fix depth normalization precision and strict loop warning

Use exact binary scaling for 24-bit depth normalization and cover the reciprocal-rounding regression. Bind the signed multiply correction pair by reference for warnings-as-errors builds.

Assisted-by: OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (implementation and verification)
Co-authored-by: capy-ai[bot] <230910855+capy-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

* ns: serve Switch 2 built-in fonts from their own shared memory

With firmware fonts the BFTTF copies fill most of the 17 MiB font
shared memory, so not even the first plain copy fit, GetBuiltInFontData
returned size 0 and Switch 2 games polled for a
font forever at boot. The plain copies now live in a separate shared
memory, created on the first GetBuiltInFontSharedMemory call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ampere: reject IADD3.X carry outputs, validate override surface buffer

The IADD3.X lowering with a third source set its carry-out from the
c addition only, missing the carry of a + b and the carry-in, and it
ignored a second carry input or output. These forms are now rejected
instead of lowered to a wrong value; none of the dumped games shaders use them.

Program overrides now bound the surface buffer in header[6] like the
texture buffer in header[4].

