=== e1d1096933
Fix the failing unit tests (incl. an AVX-512 CLZ bug) and run them in CI (#8)

* tests: fix MSVC C4388 in the ampere_sured test

The predicate check compared a size_t with an int literal. MSVC treats the
signed/unsigned mismatch (C4388) as an error, so the tests target did not
build on Windows.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (diagnosis, fix, verification and commit text)

* tests: implement batched page updates in the memory_tracker mock

FlushCachedWrites now reports coalesced ranges through
UpdatePagesCachedBatch. The mock rasterizer left that call empty, so eight
MemoryTracker cases saw no page updates. The mock now applies each range,
and the FlushCachedWrites batching case exercises the flush path.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (diagnosis, fix, verification and commit text)

* device_memory_manager: guard lookups of unregistered processes

UpdatePagesCachedCountNoLock indexed registered_processes with the ASID
stored for the page even when no process had been registered, which is an
out-of-bounds deque access. On MSVC this crashed the
"DeviceMemoryManager: UpdatePagesCachedBatch basic" test with an access
violation.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (diagnosis, fix, verification and commit text)

* tests: bind the fake cemuhook server to loopback

The server bound to 0.0.0.0 and the client sent to that address. Windows
rejects 0.0.0.0 as a destination (WSAEADDRNOTAVAIL, 10049), so
CalibrationConfigurationJob never completed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (diagnosis, fix, verification and commit text)

* dynarmic: fix VectorCountLeadingZeros16 on AVX-512

The AVX512CD path widened the eight 16-bit lanes to 32 bits in a YMM
register, counted leading zeros, then narrowed with a 128-bit vpackusdw.
That only reads the low four 32-bit results, so the upper four lanes came
back wrong on every CPU with AVX-512 (A64 CLZ.8H, e.g. Zen 4/Zen 5).
Narrow all eight with vpmovdw instead.

An exhaustive check over all 65536 inputs found 32768 mismatches before
this change and none after; the "A64: CLZ" test passes again.

