=== 514975a82e
shader_recompiler: fold max(x, -x) of merged predicate masks

Selecting a menu entry in a game lost the Vulkan device on
NVIDIA (RTX 3060, driver 621.01). One of its particle vertex shaders
takes the abs of a predicate mask as max(x, -x), where the mask was
merged from predicated moves: Phi(1 - s, -s) with s = Select(c, 0, 1).
FoldSMax32 only folded selects of two constants, so this max reached
the driver, and the draw faulted on an invalid instruction pointer.

Track the values a mask can take through selects, negations, +/-1 and
phis, and fold max(x, -x) to x & 1 when they are only -1, 0 and 1.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (debugging, implementation, message draft)
(cherry picked from commit 38230873a4a59ad9c05651e95d2d76e0cc575228)

=== da0e0ecd94
nup_container: reject directory cycles and raw extents of the wrong size

BuildDirTree walks the TOC's directory tree recursively, so a crafted
container whose directories form a cycle overflowed the stack. Allow at
most one parent per directory and none for package roots, which is what
the spec's tree shape gives.

A raw extent is the file itself (SPEC 4.1: extent_size == size); reject
records where they differ instead of serving a file of the wrong size.

