=== d30183bae7
shader: define the storage CAS write helper whenever it is used

EmitWriteStorage{U,S}{8,16} fall back to a CAS loop helper unless the
device has shaderIntN, storageBufferNBitAccess and working descriptor
aliasing. DefineWriteStorageCasLoopFunction only checked shaderInt8 and
shaderInt16, so it skipped the helper on devices that have both but
lack one of the other two.

The stock Qualcomm driver is one: shaderInt8/16 are supported, but the
device code marks descriptor aliasing as broken. Any shader with an 8
or 16-bit storage write then called an undefined function id and Sirit
aborted while building the pipeline (a game at gameplay start).
Turnip has aliasing, so it took the native path and never hit this.

Use the same conditions as the emitters, keyed on the storage buffer
types the shader actually uses.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (code)

