=== c3be47da94
video_core: copy back only CPU-read buffer pages and release held writes

Switch 2 titles do not copy GPU-written buffers back to guest memory at
fences (AsyncBufferDownloads false), which made titles that do read those
pages draw a black sky, flicker, or read stale constants: Pokemon Pokopia
builds sky, fog and exposure from GPU-computed values. Track the pages the
guest CPU actually reads (NoteCpuRead from GetFlushArea) and at a fence
copy back only the GPU writes that overlap them (QueueDownload), instead
of either everything (the per-title workaround) or nothing.

Held-back guest CPU writes to GPU-written memory are now applied on the
GPU thread before a submitted list runs (InvalidateGPUCache), and as
OnCachedWrite they copy just the changed bytes through CachedWriteMemory
rather than marking whole pages CPU-modified, which re-uploaded them over
GPU data that was never copied back.

In accurate GPU mode a release may only be waiting for the host GPU to
write it. Remember it in the query cache (PendingRelease) and let the
puller treat a semaphore acquire as met by it, so channels no longer stall
on a value that is already on its way to guest memory.

Also guard NPad::ControllerUpdate against a null applet resource, which the
input thread can hit before the HID service activates it.

Ported from Eden-NS2 15b48a6615.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 06c9f77a59
core: ignore stale page runs at unmapped pages in WalkBlock

WalkBlock sizes each step from continuity_tracker, the number of pages
after the current one that are physically contiguous with it. That count
is meaningless when the current device page is unmapped: a run left over
from an earlier mapping can make the walk skip past the unmapped page and
hand on_unmapped a block wider than the hole, losing the dialogue text
Splatoon Raiders streams through such gaps.

Treat an unmapped page as a one-page block so the walk resynchronises on
the next page instead of trusting a run that does not start at it.

Ported from Eden-NS2 bbbadec4fb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 91ec32e668
Fix Mario Kart World's black screen when a Grand Prix starts

After a movie's end-of-stream frame nothing fills a decoder image again,
but the Switch 2 video session still handed each released image a fence
value one past the syncpoint's current value. Mario Kart World releases
its images once a movie ends and waits for those fences, so a fence for a
frame that never comes hung the game on a black screen after its title
movie. A release after the stream ended, with no input and no decoded
frame queued, now completes at once with the current syncpoint value.

The session also clears that state on flush and on new input, so a
restarted stream does not inherit the old completion values.

Adds EDEN_AUTO_BUTTONS for unattended runs that have to get through
menus, from the same upstream commit.

Ported from Eden-NS2 91f7067274.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 0b31adfe7d
