=== 5116272a17
native: accept guarded uniform arithmetic and predicate combines

Patch and report by KaitonGxx, from the invisible beds and placed items
in Pokemon Pokopia.

Uniform-register instructions guarded by a UPn/!UPn execution predicate
were rejected outright, which dropped the item and preview shaders. They
are now emitted and checked afterwards: a write to R253, which holds the
guest predicate under the guard, or an unguarded write outside the
scratch registers still rejects the program, as before, but only when
the lowering actually does one.

- IMAD.X reads its carry from UPn (R239 bit 6-n) as IADD3.X does,
  instead of only carrying in P0/P1.
- UISETP 0x28c/0x88c combines with UPn (bits 74-75 select the predicate
  and the operation) instead of requiring UPT everywhere.
- the 0x887 jump-table clamp idiom no longer has to sit on UP0, and it tolerates the combine fields on both instructions.
- LEA 0xa11 high form keeps the sign bit and rejects a zero shift, which
  Maxwell would mask to no shift.

CreateGraphicsPipeline also logs the failed shader before dumping the
stages, and no longer lets the CFG throw again out of the handler, which
ended the process on the stage that failed its flow analysis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

