=== b59fd995b7
vk_pipeline_cache: reuse translated shaders between graphics pipelines

Many graphics pipelines run the same programs and differ only in fixed
function state the shaders never see (blending, depth, vertex formats).
Each one translated its programs and emitted SPIR-V again.

Translation and emission now run once per translation key: the unique
hashes of the programs, the pipeline key bits MakeRuntimeInfo reads (as
the shaders see them: attribute types, topology class, depth convention,
point size, transform feedback, tessellation, alpha test, dual source
blending) and the settings translation reads. MakeRuntimeInfo and the
layer passthrough only get that key, so nothing they read can be left
out. What translation asks the environments (constant buffer words,
texture types, viewport flag, HLE macro state) is live state outside any
key: it is recorded, and a pipeline reuses the shaders only when its own
environments give the same answers.

The cache is mutex protected and holds shared entries; the GPU thread,
the translation workers and the disk cache replay use it. On the GPU
thread, a pipeline whose shaders fit is built in place instead of being
queued for asynchronous translation. The disk cache format is unchanged.
PipelineStats counts reused pipelines, rejects and lookup time.
EDEN_NX2_SHADER_REUSE=0 turns reuse off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XYitykHUVF1YKAGcYZ8W8G
(cherry picked from commit 582c7b1bd394b038e189c43de72990bbc568b00c)

=== c404060104
vulkan: measurement-only pipeline creation timing (PipelineStats)

Measurement only, no behaviour change. Adds pipeline_stats.h: atomic
per-(thread role, graphics/compute) counters and scoped timers for native
lowering, translation (CFG + TranslateProgram + dual vertex merge), SPIR-V
emission, shader module creation and the driver pipeline compile, plus
counts of pipelines, repeated shader-hash combinations and repeated
(stage, hash) translations. Roles: gpu, xlate (translation_workers),
par (workers running the queued driver compile), boot (disk cache replay).
One LOG_INFO line per active role/kind every 10 s plus totals since boot.
Disable with EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_STATS=0.

