nx2: page runs, sparse residency rollback, GPU-written command lists

Map and Unmap cut the memory page runs first: the old runs made a later read
see the previous mapping, or zeros. A sparse bind that cannot place its mip
tail releases the layers it just allocated instead of leaking them. Command
lists the GPU writes are marked written and read back from the GPU's copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 8068e15e76
yuzu_cmd: skip the kernel teardown when nothing was started; android: quick settings

eden-cli reset the kernel on exit even after it had exited early, which shut
down services that never came up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 57cb8bb1a4
gpu: deferred instance state, and drain the split before reading it

Draws that follow a macro's state writes take the instance state written
after the macro loop. The split thread also gets one more pass to finish its
queued work before the front thread reads the caches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 9c890a01b0
am: apply docked and handheld to Switch 2 titles only

The docked/handheld state follows the console's own switches for NS2
titles; on Switch 1 titles the change makes the reported mode jump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 0dcd7b9f0e
build: skip the fork-only checks on a fork, add the PayPal button

tx-src and Check Strings run on a self-hosted runner labelled "source" that
belongs to eden-emu/eden. On a fork they queued forever and the release page
listed them as failed checks. Gate both on the repository, and add the
donation link to the README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== f285120497
texture_cache: native tilings view header, and drop MSVC 4388/4389 as errors

IsValidEntry built its ImageInfo without the view header that native tiling
needs, so the guest size came out wrong for Switch 2 titles. Also cast the
layer index before the multiply, and stop treating signed/unsigned mismatch
warnings as errors in MSVC builds (the tree does not compile with them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 76df4591a7
vk_rasterizer: perform the indirect draw reset program's stores

Donkey Kong Bananza resets each terrain piece's indirect draw record through
pointers loaded from memory. Stores to addresses read from memory cannot be
mapped onto a storage buffer, so the recompiler loses them, every record keeps
zero copies and the draw draws nothing. Recognise that program and do its
stores here. EDEN_NX2_RESETFIX=0 leaves them to the GPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 5a9573121e
dma_pusher: flush macro parameters the GPU wrote

A macro's parameters can continue into an entry of their own, and there they
are arguments the GPU wrote: Donkey Kong Bananza's terrain counts each mesh in
an indirect draw record and draws with it, so the macro read the older guest
words and nothing was drawn. Flush the small parameter blocks before the
macro reads them. EDEN_NX2_PBFLUSH=0 turns this off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 07c017f1d3
shader: FSEL sources keep .NEG/.ABS, and native array-cube vector samples

FSEL shared the bitwise SEL case and so dropped the negation and absolute
bits of its sources. Ampere TXD/TLD with dimension 7, LOD 3 and up to four
components is a native array-cube vector sample; lower it to the two-operand
Maxwell form when the instruction fits and refuse it otherwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 78bc9aa114
nx2: read EDEN_NX2_* switches from nx2_switches.txt at startup

A launch from the GUI cannot set environment variables, so the EDEN_NX2_*
switches were only reachable from a shell. Read them from nx2_switches.txt
next to the executable, then from %APPDATA%\eden\nx2_switches.txt; a variable
already in the real environment wins over both. The build copies dist copies
of the file next to the binary, so every package carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== a5c06ea209
nx2: copy buffers back for titles that read GPU-written data

AsyncBufferDownloads is off for native tiling, which left Pokemon Pokopia's
sky black or flickering: its guest side reads buffer data the CPU never
touches, so the fence-time copy-back is the only path that produces it.
Keep the default off and name the titles that need it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

