=== 9abbf8296d
shader_recompiler: run the destructors of pooled objects

ObjectPool's Chunk::Release destroyed the Storage union elements, whose
destructor is empty, so the pooled objects' own destructors never ran:
every shader build leaked the heap memory IR instructions own (phi
operand lists of more than two entries, AssociatedInsts). Release now
destroys each used object. Shader pools are released blocks first, then
instructions, so destroying a block's instruction list only unlinks
instructions that are still alive.

