=== b7ff03036c
nx2: support mapping modify so NVN2 places compressible textures

NVN2 gives a texture in a compressible memory pool its GPU address only
after NvRmGpuMappingModify switched the pool's mapping to the texture's
kind. NvRm fails that call unless the GPU characteristics report
NVGPU_GPU_FLAGS_SUPPORT_MAPPING_MODIFY, so such textures kept address 0
and draws into them went nowhere: title 1's cup-opening movie stayed on
its first frame (also its 640x360 and 512x512 passes).

Report the flag and answer the request nn::gpu::sdk then sends, gpu
sub-session 212 (NormalModifyMemoryKind4K), with the wanted kind and a
signalled job slot. The movie now plays on screen and the race follows.

=== 371d03f160
kernel: Switch 2 processes get an 8 GiB larger heap region

nninitStartup asks for ~9.5 GiB (total memory minus ~6.3 GiB), past the
8 GiB 39-bit heap region, so SetHeapSize failed with OutOfMemory.

