Notes: rows 105-109 (video sessions, interpreter, GPU ASTC transcode, present serialization, job-system SVCs)

=== 65a52cffa5
nx2: video decoder sessions; present waits on an event; present timeline

- gsv 901/1001 succeed and 902/1002 return sessions; their TIPC 1
  (CreateVideoDecoderService) returns another, auto-stubbed. Title 1's
  movie player no longer aborts with 2001-0114 (no frames are decoded).
- The present's wait for its fence is woken by the GPU thread through a
  syncpoint action instead of 200 us sleeps (~1 ms each on Windows).
- Every 600 presents, log the average frame time and how much of it the
  present thread spent blocked on the GPU fence, compositing and pacing.

=== 1522ce5e43
ASTC: decode and re-compress to BC1/BC3 on the GPU; texture cache budget

- accelerate_astc=Gpu with astc_recompression=Bc1/Bc3 now decodes ASTC
  with the GPU decoder into a temporary RGBA8 image (dedicated memory,
  freed once the GPU is past it) and compresses it with a new compute
  shader (bc_encoder.comp: bounding-box endpoints along the colours'
  covariance, inset 1/16, nearest palette entry; BC3 alpha ramp; BC1
  punch-through), then copies the blocks into the image. No CPU decode,
  so streamed textures are ready the frame they are first used instead
  of showing placeholders for seconds; the decode pass no longer waits
  for the GPU on this path.
- The CPU path (CpuAsynchronous) fills a new image with zero blocks
  before its first decode instead of showing stale VRAM, and the
  transcode pool is a quarter of the hardware threads.
- Switch 2 titles: collector thresholds near the device budget, re-read
  every 60 frames from VK_EXT_memory_budget (another game shrank it from
  7.0 to 5.4 GB).
- EDEN_NX2_HIDE_WINDOW=0 now leaves the window visible.

=== 9686a8f94b
Native MME: decode each instruction once; reuse the parameter FIFO

The Turing macro interpreter re-extracted every field of each 96-bit
instruction on every execution and copied the register file per
instruction; title 1's GPU thread spent about half its busy time there.
Instructions are now decoded once per PC (re-decoded when their words
change) and both lanes' operands are read up front instead of copying
the registers. The parameter FIFO is a member instead of a vector
allocated per macro call. Rendering checked unchanged on the attract
loop; the GPU thread went from ~68% to ~45-50% busy.

=== 69e7033d82
Texture cache: stop the churn, the per-frame image leak and garbage textures

- Unmapped GPU addresses get a stand-in CPU address fixed by the GPU
  address. A fresh one per lookup meant FindImage never found an image
  there again: title 1's bloom chain at 0xf0000-0x15b600 was re-created
  on every use (~5,400 images per 600 frames), filling VRAM.
- ASTC whose blocks carry no alpha (exact endpoint-mode scan reusing the
  decoder's block parsing) is re-compressed to BC1 instead of BC3, half
  the size; about 70% of title 1's ASTC qualifies. Copies between BC1
  and BC3 hosts are skipped (their guest data is uploaded instead).
  EDEN_NX2_ASTC_BC1=0 turns it off.
- Deleting an image cancels every decode still queued for it. An image
  re-decoded mid-decode has two; the first to finish cleared IsDecoding,
  the second was not cancelled and was uploaded into the next image to
  take the slot: garbage textures (the title logo, road patches) and a
  staging overrun when that image was smaller.
- Diagnostics: images created and deleted per 600 frames by shape,
  collector deletions, async decodes, BC1/BC3 split; collector
  thresholds overridable (EDEN_NX2_TC_EXPECTED_MIB/CRITICAL_MIB); GPU
  ASTC decode wait timing (EDEN_NX2_ASTC_FLUSH=1 submits without it).

Title 1 attract loop: device memory 4.8-5.1 GB instead of 5.9-6.1 GB, no
decoded textures evicted, ~17 -> 22-23 fps.

