=== 9a86143287
Notes: row 102 resolved (async decode use-after-free)

=== 5505e1ddae
Texture cache: fix use-after-free in async texture decode

TickAsyncDecode locked a finished decode's mutex, erased the context (freeing
the mutex) and only then let the lock go out of scope, unlocking freed
memory. With ASTC re-compressed on the CPU (accelerate_astc=CpuAsynchronous)
title 1 hit this a few minutes in: cdb reported "Free Heap block modified
after it was freed" at the mutex offset, and a run without the debugger
crashed. The lock is now released before the erase.

Also, deleting an image while it is being decoded (deletions other than the
collector, which already skips them) cancels the decode instead of
uploading into a freed slot.

Verified under cdb past 330 s (failed at 243 s twice before).

=== 9677090712
nx2 services: callbacks no longer outlive their sessions

Under cdb title 1 reported "Free Heap block modified after it was freed"
when it recreated its display session (~4 min in); a run without the
debugger crashed at 113 s. The vi2 vsync timer callback (HostTiming thread)
captured the session and signalled its events; the destructor unscheduled
the timer (which does not wait for a running callback) and closed the
events. The syncpt slot actions (GPU thread) had the same race with
CloseEvent, as did the frame-capture and dump callbacks.

vsync events now live in state shared with the callback and are emptied
under its lock before closing; syncpt actions check a shared "alive" flag
under a mutex the destructor takes; capture/dump callbacks hold no session
pointers.

