Switch 2: Turing macros, native compute, Ampere shader lowering, native tiling

From changes.patch: the TU104/GA10x MME interpreter (shared macro context for
the process's channels, also on the compute class), native compute with QMD
3.0 dependency scheduling, the Ampere-to-Maxwell shader lowering, native
vertex stream sizes, and the console's GOB swizzle for textures, DMA copies
and the host unswizzle shaders. Switch 2 channels turn all of it on at init.

